WEBVTT

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.880
Citizens of Fort Severn.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.970
As your mayor, I wish to promise you that this peace will last forever.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.730
No matter what underhanded tactics that the mobile suit pilots...

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.770
...and Vultures who infest this devastated postwar world might use to attack us,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.940
we have among us a mighty power!

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.030
And that power is the leader of Fort Severn's self-defense force,

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.910
the Newtype Carris Nautilus!

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:53.340
Long ago, when mankind had just begun to dwell in space,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.930
there appeared in their midst people with new abilities...

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.390
...that no one had ever possessed before.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.560
These people, with their superior judgment and keen insight,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.350
were seen as what all humanity should aspire to be reformed into,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.190
and came to be called Newtypes.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.070
In the recent war, however, the power of Newtypes was exploited in battle,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.080
and as a result, the human race was brought to the brink of extinction.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.370
It is also said that most Newtypes perished.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.880
But I was born with the same abilities as those people.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.630
Indeed, I am a new Newtype, one born into the postwar world.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.350
I will devote my abilities to the cause of peace.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.890
I believe that to be the best way to make atonement to my brothers,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.640
whose lives were lost in that terrible war.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.900
Citizens! You heard his words!

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:57.700
As long as Carris Nautilus is here, our peaceful lives will continue forever!

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.860
<b>After War</b>

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.860
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:19.340
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.300
<b>little by little</b>

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.850
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:34.230
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:43.740
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.290
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.290
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.920
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.840
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.470
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:06.350
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.890
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:15.770
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.980
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.980
<b>"I Am a Newtype"</b>

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:32.330
One week has passed since Tiffa Adill drew that picture.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.920
Jamil has the Freeden set course for Fort Severn,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.130
a northern city that they believe to be the one in the drawing.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:44.590
Naturally, his goal is to meet the Newtype he believes is there.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.640
If we keep up this pace, we should reach our destination ahead of schedule.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:53.310
I'm amazed that you figured out the location from just one drawing!

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.810
The picture Tiffa drew was pretty accurate.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.030
It was a perfect match for photos of Fort Severn.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.200
So we'll find the Newtype who lives there, and-

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.450
Hang on, what do we do after we find him?

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.620
It depends on the situation.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.540
However, there are many who would try to exploit a Newtype's powers.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.000
If he requires sanctuary, we will offer it to him.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.630
If need be, we might take him on as a Freeden crew member like Tiffa.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.380
If this person's abilities are already being misused by someone,

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.300
more drastic steps might be called for.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.260
If necessary, yes.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:31.850
But if the Newtype is the bad guy, that won't even be funny, am I right?

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.770
That is my greatest worry.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.030
If we have to fight a Newtype, we must be prepared for a difficult battle.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.280
Oh, right...

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.240
Hey, there's nothing to worry about!

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.870
We have three world-class Gundams with us!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.040
Answer me this!

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.250
When operating a Gundam in a cold climate, what maintenance is required?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.130
Put antifreeze in each manipulator's fluid pulse system.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:07.130
You'd also have to replace the sealant resin.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.930
No, you'd have to miniaturize the engine's radiator first.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.430
All are correct!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:18.650
But there are 25 other correct answers. Try to find them all yourselves!

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:19.400
Later!

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.730
No way! No way!

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.190
Hey, Gundam Boy!

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.360
What did you want to talk to me about, Obnoxious Brat?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.200
Did you ask Jamil about what I said?

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.030
Nope.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.030
Why not?!

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.580
It's not like we need to upgrade the GX anymore, right?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.120
As long as it has the Satellite System, the GX is invincible.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.120
But what if the Moon isn't out?

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.290
We have the Leopard and Airmaster.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.130
In urban combat, a heavy-caliber, high output weapon like the Satellite Cannon-

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.720
I've been training in standard combat.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.850
But what about... What about...

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.930
Come on, I can see right through you.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:57.980
Make all the excuses you want, you really just want to tinker with my GX!

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.230
Please! I've got a ton of awesome parts that I've been setting aside!

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.900
I couldn't possibly sell 'em off without using them!

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:08.530
Awesome parts? What, you mean those?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.570
I sure do!

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.330
Look at these beauties!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:20.460
This is a twin-mount mega particle beam cannon from an old U.N.E. warship!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.630
And this is a multiple-linked, anti-mobile suit gun...

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:27.170
...from an old S.R.A. armored vehicle, aka a "Harmonica"!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.760
That's an expandable shield sub-frame that never made it past prototyping.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.600
And this fella is a large-bore thruster meant for a mobile armor!

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:39.440
Come on, doesn't the thought of mounting this stuff on the GX...

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.770
...get your heart pumping?!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.570
Even if you beg me later, I'm not gonna put 'em on, you hear?

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.790
That one goes over there. Maybe a bit to the left for that one.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.620
Hey, be careful with that!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.330
It's an antique!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:08.670
Hey!

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.100
I'm gonna put this on display somewhere.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.640
Let's see, where would be good?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:19.810
That's the spot!

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.310
Wow, that's ugly.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.110
Did you say something?

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.650
Just that you have exquisite taste!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.070
What'cha doing?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.530
Wow, what's all this?!

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:33.360
It's a long-term contract, so I used my own money...

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.330
...to pick up a few things so I wouldn't get bored.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:39.660
I figured I'd put together a rec room that everyone could use.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.120
Wow, that's awfully nice of you!

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:45.290
It'll be a membership system, so dues will be collected, of course.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.630
And there it is...

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.130
Hey, I know!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.800
What's with him?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.720
His actions are as plain as day to me.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.100
Hey, do you think I'm a Newtype?

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.060
Moron. I have a pretty good idea, too.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.890
Oops!

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.900
Tiffa! Tiffa, are you there?

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:21.500
What the heck happened in here?! This is amazing!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.170
Did the Captain authorize this?

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.420
I was planning to get it right now.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:28.630
I see.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:32.340
Personally, I think it's a great idea to have a place like this!

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.800
What a great sofa! Look!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.970
I should've known there'd be trouble.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.020
Ladies get free membership.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.230
Do that, and I'll get authorization from the Captain.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:50.690
You have a deal.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.860
Okay. I'll go put in a word with him.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.240
Something seems different about her.

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:03.120
Anyway, isn't it great that you got permission?

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.830
What is that?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.710
It's hideous!

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.550
So sue me!

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.430
As agreed, my membership is free.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.180
You crooked quack!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.940
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.020
What, everybody's here?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.030
C'mon in!

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.030
Hurry!

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.740
You have a date, huh? Way to go!

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.620
The VIP seat is open.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.710
Honestly, kids these days are such a handful.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.630
Get off my case! Cut it out!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.550
So, what about their membership fees?

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.420
I guess it'll be free for kids under 15.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.840
Nobody's paying anything...

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.310
Tiffa? Is something wrong?

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.940
No, it's... nothing.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:16.240
Well, if you say so.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.350
You'll catch cold if you stay out here.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.230
I know.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:52.480
Can you sense that Newtype?

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.940
Yes, but only faintly.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.820
I see.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:01.360
Garrod?

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:04.160
It's nothing!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:12.460
When you're done, come inside! It's too cold for me out here!

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.460
Someone with the same powers as you?

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.170
I'm positive.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.010
The time is finally upon us.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.560
Postwar chaos that shows no sign of abating.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.900
People fighting and hurting one another.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:47.490
To put an end to such a foolish era, great power is called for.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.410
And this mobile armor, the Patulia, is that power.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.540
If we can activate the Patulia,

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.630
the unification of the postwar world will be within our reach.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.510
Yes, but tremendous Newtype power will be required to do so.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.630
I know. That is why I-

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.760
Yes, of course.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.430
Let me go collect the Newtype who is coming this way.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.440
Depending on how it goes, force of arms might be required.

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:19.070
If you must. However, the people of Fort Severn mustn't learn of this project.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.570
Is that clear, Carris?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:24.410
Crystal clear, Mayor Nomoa.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.500
We can put an end to this foolish era with my power.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.580
With my power...

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:07.910
It was a dream. Wasn't it?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.640
A Vulture ship? Sure, I passed by one a while ago.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.720
It was headed towards Fort Severn.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.220
Thanks.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.310
Fort Severn, huh?

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.440
What? The ship is going to be ambushed, you say?

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.780
Freeden, halt!

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.330
Anything on radar?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.000
It's useless, it's all a jumble!

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:59.540
All hands to battle stations! Put the Gundams on standby!

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:03.340
Tiffa!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.050
What got into her?

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.100
I've never seen her run before.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:15.060
What? I shouldn't go into battle?

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.940
It's a request from your sweetie.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.310
Shouldn't you do as she says?

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.690
Pay me a little something, and I'll do your share.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:27.400
Go on, shoo!

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:31.450
If you've got time for chit-chat, you've got time for final cockpit checks!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:35.330
If I do go out, what will happen to me?

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:38.620
You... will lose.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.630
I don't see anything.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:52.300
How about you? See anything?

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:53.850
No, nothing.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.220
How about you?

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:56.890
Nothing here, either.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:01.730
What is it?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.820
I could swear I just saw people snowboarding...

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.190
They're here!

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.490
All Gundams, please scramble.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.960
Let go, Tiffa! I'm going, too!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.040
No!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.790
I believe your vision, but I want to try to overcome it.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:30.630
Garrod...

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:37.850
GX, heading out!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:48.690
They've got guts, attacking the ship unprovoked like this.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.070
Are they Vultures?

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.820
No, Boarders.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.910
Let's go greet them!

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:56.780
Wait!

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.160
You idiot!

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.120
We tried to warn you!

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:03.830
Oh, crap!

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.380
My visibility is shot!

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.260
I can't lose...

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.010
If I get beaten here, I'll lose Tiffa again!

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:20.720
No way am I gonna lose!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.030
Garrod!

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.030
Bastards!

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.830
I can't lose... I won't lose!

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:50.880
Garrod isn't fighting the enemy out there.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.430
He's fighting against the word "Newtype."

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:56.800
Yes.

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:00.180
What is it, Tiffa?

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.230
He's coming.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.610
Please keep them occupied, everyone.

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.450
What's he...? Come back here!

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.490
Garrod!

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.800
Tiffa!

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.730
I won't let you lay a finger on that ship!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.400
I'm searching for one of my kind. I'll thank you to not interfere.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.440
One of your kind?

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:55.780
No way... No way, you're-

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.820
Yes. I am a Newtype.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.120
Ah, so it's you. What is your name?

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.170
S-Stop it!

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:12.670
Tiffa. Tiffa Adill, is it?

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.420
Why, you...!

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:23.970
It's no use. You can't defeat me, not even in a Gundam.

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:27.730
Shove it! If you're a Newtype, all the more reason I can't lose to you!

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:30.730
Run, Garrod...

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:34.150
You can't beat him as you are now.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:46.580
Oh, is that how it is? I'll make use of you, then.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.000
To help me get Tiffa.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.170
W-What?

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:01.720
What are those?

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:12.940
Well, Tiffa? You can see the future, can't you?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.440
Stop it!

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:17.190
Prepare to fire main guns! Give the GX support fire!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:18.690
Yes, sir!

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.080
It's no use.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:31.580
That mobile suit is definitely a Bertigo.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:36.340
But that doesn't matter. It's that boy's death that I came here to see.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.430
I'm still holding back.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.190
This certainly stinks...

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:04.110
Garrod, hold out until we can get there to help you.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.330
Bastards!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:25.760
This is the power of a Newtype?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:27.970
Garrod!

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.100
Watch closely, Tiffa.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:35.400
I'll destroy the Gundam.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.900
No, don't!

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.660
Yes! This is what I came to see!

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.330
Everyone who spurns me deserves to die!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.660
Garrod!

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.960
I said it is no use.

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:44.630
What?! What?!

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:55.020
Humans without special powers can't possibly beat me!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:02.400
For the happiness of all, to create a world full of bliss,

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.990
I will make use of your life.

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:07.030
Garrod, what are you doing?

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:09.530
Get up! Get on your feet!

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:10.820
Run Garrod!

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:11.990
You'll be killed!

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:14.040
Garrod!

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:17.500
Come on, get on with it! Finish him off!

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:29.930
You said something fascinating earlier.

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:33.430
That my being a Newtype is all the more reason for you not to lose.

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:37.390
I'm sorry, but reality is cruel.

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:40.850
Old humanity can't beat me!

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:43.770
Garrod!

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.990
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:51.480
Ironically, Carris, the Newtype they had sought,

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:56.370
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:53.880
lashed out at Garrod.

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:59.080
Two people who hunger for revenge plot behind the scenes of this battle.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:04.210
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:03.930
Garrod is overwhelmed, and Jamil does something to strengthen his resolve.

00:23:04.930 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:17.550
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.440
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:22.420
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:26.480
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:31.400
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.530
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:37.590
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:39.580
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.710
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.080
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:48.420
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:52.240
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:51.840
Don't think, just run!

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:56.440
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:56.440
<b>"Don't Think, Just Run!"</b>

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:58.440
<b></b>
